## Item 05: soundness of the fixed solver (2026-10-01)

**The answer: no failure anywhere.** The
  > $ cd /home/al/dev/MOSP; sed -i 's/^- \[ \] \*\*05 Soundness of the fixed solver\.\*\*/- [x] **05 Soundness of the fixed solver.**/' Ralph_Loops/loop0007/iteration
  > $ ps -eo pid,args | grep solver_fix_soundness | grep -v grep | head

Item 05 is done and marked `[x]`. Nothing failed anywhere: no certified value changed and no false refutation turned up. The gate passes (1,345 MOSP tests, 110 pathwidth_solver tests).

**The whole search, rewritten from the theorems.** I added `paper2/solver_fix_soundness.py`. It contains a second copy of the search with the two repairs written straight from the Lean statements. It uses only functions from `paper2/search_check.py`. In particular, the "hereditarily definite" test there works by listing every intermediate set, so the C and Python matching code are checked against an independent method. Each run is compared four ways: with the exact answer, with node soundness at every node it expands, with the C (answer and node count), and with the production Python.
- **Coverage:** 17,431,232 runs over 52,592 graphs at 1–17 vertices, under all 64 rule settings. That includes every labelled graph up to 6 vertices, every 7-vertex graph, random graphs at 8–13, the known counterexamples, and 12,000 graphs from the hunt's counterexample-prone family at 12–17.
- **Result:** zero wrong answers, zero lost nodes (51.5 M checked), and zero mismatches with the C or the Python.
- **The check can tell the rule sets apart:** 4,203 of these runs come out differently under the published rules. So agreement with the C shows the C really runs the repaired rules.

**Differential harness, with the new defaults.** I ran it on every certified instance, not a sample: 43,935 at 9–40 customers (1.76 M calls) and 1,231 at 50–75 (29,544 calls). It found zero disagreements, contradictions or witness failures, and no call hit its deadline. The independent small-instance oracle agrees on all 13,612 instances it can check.

**Corpus.** `benchmarks.corpus` still reads 6,374 of 6,376 certified, and `solutions/` is unchanged against HEAD.

**Not covered:** 76–125 customers. Item 04's paired refutations remain the only record there.

**One thing to watch:** the committed `learning/data/ensemble/differential.csv.gz` shows +2.5% refutation nodes against today's run at n ≤ 40. Item 04's paired measurement of the repair's cost is +0.004%. So that file must come from older code and shouldn't be read as what the repair costs.

The write-up is the "Item 05" section of `paper2/solver_fix.md`, and the status line at the top of that file now records item 05's result. The results are in `paper2/data/solver_fix_soundness_*` and `paper2/data/solver_fix_diff{40,75}*`; I wrote nothing over the committed differential files. I added one test, `test_the_c_runs_the_repaired_search_as_the_theorems_state_it`, to `tests/test_repaired_rules.py`. PROGRESS.md is updated to 5/10. Nothing is committed, as instructed.

